{:edb/db-before-t 2457 :edb/db-after-t 2458 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535770 50 #inst "2026-10-09T06:51:47.988Z" 13194139535770 true] [17592186133839 1020 #edb/ref 17592186365376 13194139535770 true] [17592186133846 1020 #edb/ref 17592186365383 13194139535770 true] [17592186133848 1020 #edb/ref 17592186365390 13194139535770 true] [17592186133848 1020 #edb/ref 17592186365397 13194139535770 true] [17592186134216 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535770 true] [17592186134216 1100 "Evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}2x\\,\\text{d}V\n$$\n\nwhere $R$ is the type III region given by \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,{x}^{2}\\le z\\le 2{x}^{2},\\,0\\le y\\le 2xz}.\n$$" 13194139535770 true] [17592186134216 1100 "Evaluate the triple integral\n\n$∭_(R)2xdV$\n\nwhere $R$ is the type III region given by\n\n$R = {(x, y, z): 0 \\le x \\le 1, x^{2} \\le z \\le 2x^{2}, 0 \\le y \\le 2xz}$." 13194139535770 false] [17592186134216 1145 "Writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}2x\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{2{x}^{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{2xz}2x\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y$, treating $x$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{2{x}^{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{2xz}2x\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{2{x}^{2}}[{\\int }_{0}^{2xz}2x\\,dy]dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{2{x}^{2}}2x[y]_{y=0}^{y=2xz}dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{2{x}^{2}}2x(2xz)\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{2{x}^{2}}4{x}^{2}z\\,dz\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{2{x}^{2}}4{x}^{2}z\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{2{x}^{2}}4{x}^{2}z\\,dz]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2{x}^{2}[{z}^{2}]_{z={x}^{2}}^{z=2{x}^{2}}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2{x}^{2}((2{x}^{2})^{2}-({x}^{2})^{2})dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}6{x}^{6}\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}6{x}^{6}\\,dx & ={[\\frac{6{x}^{7}}{7}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365376 1017 #edb/ref 17592186365377 13194139535770 true] [17592186365376 1089 "q-161707" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365376 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535770 true] [17592186365376 1100 "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{8}z\\,dy]dA\n$$\n\ngiven that the region $D$ in the $xz$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD={(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le 4}.\n$$" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365376 1113 #uuid "99d7aeb0-f499-5945-8df6-2ed6bcdeb02c" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365376 1145 "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y,$ treating $x$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}z\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{D}z[y]_{y={x}^{3}}^{y=8}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}z(8-{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type I region in the $xz$-plane.\nTherefore, to evaluate our double integral as a repeated integral over this region, we integrate with respect to $z$ and then with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}z(8-{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{4}z(8-{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(8-{x}^{3})[{\\int }_{0}^{4}z\\,\\text{d}z]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(8-{x}^{3}){[\\frac{{z}^{2}}{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=4}\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}8(8-{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8{[8x-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}]}_{z=0}^{z=2} \\\\  & =8(16-4) \\\\  & =96\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365377 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365378 13194139535770 true] [17592186365377 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365379 13194139535770 true] [17592186365377 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365380 13194139535770 true] [17592186365377 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365381 13194139535770 true] [17592186365377 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365382 13194139535770 true] [17592186365377 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535770 true] [17592186365377 1041 "selection" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365377 1104 #edb/ref 17592186365381 13194139535770 true] [17592186365377 1110 #uuid "27f1bac3-5478-5043-b94f-4b5e882a771d" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365378 1034 "92" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365378 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535770 true] [17592186365378 1111 #uuid "1435e028-99d2-5627-b830-911174be3e37" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365379 1034 "84" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365379 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535770 true] [17592186365379 1111 #uuid "9e993d76-5d6e-5f57-bba0-265da0bc8945" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365380 1034 "88" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365380 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535770 true] [17592186365380 1111 #uuid "49840418-28a8-5eca-8345-fbb5b95e6529" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365381 1034 "96" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365381 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535770 true] [17592186365381 1111 #uuid "42f4146c-1875-5481-aa6e-e32e3c2c16b0" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365382 1034 "98" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365382 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535770 true] [17592186365382 1111 #uuid "00d55826-3190-5a37-a80a-04f64ab94c98" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365383 1017 #edb/ref 17592186365384 13194139535770 true] [17592186365383 1089 "q-161781" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365383 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535770 true] [17592186365383 1100 "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}6y\\,dV\n$$\n\nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,x\\le y\\le 1-z},\n$$\n\nand $D$ is a finite region in $xz$-plane enclosed between the $x$-axis, the $z$-axis,  and the curve $z=1-x$ in the first quadrant." 13194139535770 true] [17592186365383 1113 #uuid "62ec7383-3add-5783-838d-5ccce9844f89" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365383 1145 "Writing down our triple integral as a mixed integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}6y\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{x}^{1-z}6y\\,dy]dA.\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y,$ treating $x$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{x}^{1-z}6y\\,dy]dA & ={∬}_{D}3[{y}^{2}]_{y=x}^{y=1-z}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}3((1-z)^{2}-{x}^{2})\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe must now evaluate this double integral over the region $D$ in the $xz$-plane shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070114/assets/819b5b00967bf485068c146602bf962481b21b75d5319113fd6bd94366e84be0.png)\n\n \n\nWe can evaluate our double integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}3((1-z)^{2}-{x}^{2})\\,dA & ={∬}_{D}3((1-z)^{2}-{x}^{2})\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}3((1-z)^{2}-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[-(1-z)^{3}]}_{z=0}^{z=1-x}-3{x}^{2}[z]_{z=0}^{z=1-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}-{x}^{3}+1-3{x}^{2}(1-x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\,\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-{x}^{3}+x]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =(\\,\\frac{1}{2}-1+1)-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365384 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365385 13194139535770 true] [17592186365384 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365386 13194139535770 true] [17592186365384 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365387 13194139535770 true] [17592186365384 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365388 13194139535770 true] [17592186365384 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365389 13194139535770 true] [17592186365384 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535770 true] [17592186365384 1041 "selection" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365384 1104 #edb/ref 17592186365386 13194139535770 true] [17592186365384 1110 #uuid "71963b0e-cb06-5435-90a3-bd88b0dc18b6" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365385 1034 "\\frac{5}{6}" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365385 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535770 true] [17592186365385 1111 #uuid "9b3b0ebc-7d21-5c71-a721-332d43af1174" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365386 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365386 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535770 true] [17592186365386 1111 #uuid "7a060360-f156-5748-aff7-a371cead9a02" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365387 1034 "\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365387 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535770 true] [17592186365387 1111 #uuid "a14914d8-167e-54df-abc7-7cd270fbff56" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365388 1034 "1" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365388 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535770 true] [17592186365388 1111 #uuid "a78fa246-c089-53e2-a15c-5dbe923a5fb2" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365389 1034 "\\frac{3}{4}" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365389 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535770 true] [17592186365389 1111 #uuid "e1ea7d75-5311-56b3-82e1-01e10e2e95c1" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365390 1017 #edb/ref 17592186365391 13194139535770 true] [17592186365390 1089 "q-161853" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365390 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535770 true] [17592186365390 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070114/assets/a1e4a1e39c85a037f3f4f49910b651300363ef34bee969464f5e711aa00986e3.png)\n\nEvaluate the triple integral \n${∭}_{R}4{x}^{2}z\\,dV$\nover the region $R,$ shown above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the right one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365390 1113 #uuid "86b32cbc-034e-5e5d-a572-7bdac44abc92" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365390 1145 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070114/assets/9165163be9ce95e7165f04d26e6ce8080699ab4d477eba3f804c849fdf1fb679.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type III region\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 4-z},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD={(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 3}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $xz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070114/assets/ca74bf149c1371fe9f1622586d9eb92fe180a9c9bb6a0c53d16f538b3c55f4a4.png)\n\nHence, the type III representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 4-z}\n$$\n\nAs a result, by writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}4{x}^{2}z\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4-z}4{x}^{2}z\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y$, treating $x$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4-z}4{x}^{2}z\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{4-z}4{x}^{2}z\\,dy]dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}4{x}^{2}z[y]_{y=0}^{y=4-z}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}4{x}^{2}z(4-z)\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(16{x}^{2}z-4{x}^{2}{z}^{2})\\,dz\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(16{x}^{2}z-4{x}^{2}{z}^{2})\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{3}(16{x}^{2}z-4{x}^{2}{z}^{2})\\,dz]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[8{x}^{2}{z}^{2}-\\frac{4}{3}{x}^{2}{z}^{3}]_{z=0}^{z=3}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}36{x}^{2}\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}36{x}^{2}\\,dx & ={[12{x}^{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =(12-0) \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365391 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365392 13194139535770 true] [17592186365391 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365393 13194139535770 true] [17592186365391 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365394 13194139535770 true] [17592186365391 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365395 13194139535770 true] [17592186365391 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365396 13194139535770 true] [17592186365391 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535770 true] [17592186365391 1041 "selection" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365391 1104 #edb/ref 17592186365392 13194139535770 true] [17592186365391 1110 #uuid "64ab83e3-34fe-58d5-af51-8fbbc1cca887" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365392 1034 "12" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365392 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535770 true] [17592186365392 1111 #uuid "1ecea781-e9c8-5466-9fdd-87247b399b19" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365393 1034 "2" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365393 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535770 true] [17592186365393 1111 #uuid "48018ee4-99b8-5569-8237-2eac9f1f6af5" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365394 1034 "6" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365394 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535770 true] [17592186365394 1111 #uuid "1e172e0f-2815-58d5-876f-c1d82ada6dd3" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365395 1034 "1" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365395 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535770 true] [17592186365395 1111 #uuid "23ab1ed5-f014-50fa-95a5-86d98fd53cc9" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365396 1034 "24" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365396 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535770 true] [17592186365396 1111 #uuid "43e1218d-1686-5faf-a74d-aa659e7074f4" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365397 1017 #edb/ref 17592186365398 13194139535770 true] [17592186365397 1089 "q-163717" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365397 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535770 true] [17592186365397 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070114/assets/4be9362c014a7b8f0d0708ca5d7ea32a1b5bb13d48e2e1704341d04b89f9566a.png)\n\nGiven that $R$ is the type III region shown above, \n${∭}_{R}\\frac{\\pi x}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{\\pi y}{4}\\,\\text{d}V=$" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365397 1113 #uuid "98d947ff-3e63-571a-956d-fa65049b909f" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365397 1145 "For a type III region $R$ with projection $D$ onto the $xz$-plane, the triple integral of a continuous function $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(x,z)}^{{u}_{2}(x,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe consider the region $R$ as a type III region enclosed between the back surface $y={u}_{1}(x,z)=0$ and the front surface $y={u}_{2}(x,z)=2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070114/assets/63cffdee00edd80c4a0abdc30e8e45b1af29078b8bc4902bf3f60b7b4a104172.png)\n\nSo, the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we consider the projection $D$ as a type II *plane* region in the $xz$-plane with the right curve\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{ln}⁡z.\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070114/assets/dc72aeb4b554d88f00083dc6bf6f8ca4244e1b7683c8dec10ba0491c678a5603.png)\n\nHence, $D={(x,z)\\,:\\,1\\le z\\le e,\\,0\\le x\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡z}.$\n\nTherefore, we write the triple integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}\\frac{\\pi x}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{\\pi y}{4}\\,\\text{d}V & ={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{\\pi x}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{\\pi y}{4}\\text{d}y]\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}x[{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{\\pi y}{4}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}x{[\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi y}{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}x\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535770 true] [17592186365398 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365399 13194139535770 true] [17592186365398 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365400 13194139535770 true] [17592186365398 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365401 13194139535770 t